issues.problematic_code_snippet:
smtp = (smtplib.SMTP_SSL if (self.use_tls and not self.opportunistic_tls) else smtplib.SMTP)(
    self.server, self.port, timeout=10, local_hostname=local_host or None
)

findings.body:
With `SMTP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME` unset, `local_host` is `""`, and `smtp.ehlo(local_host)` falls back to `smtplib`'s `self.local_hostname`, which is the machine FQDN. The base code deliberately sent `ehlo(self.server)` ("HELO domain name as the server address") both before and after STARTTLS. Every existing deployment using opportunistic TLS therefore starts presenting a different HELO/EHLO identity after this upgrade, with no config change on their side. Some relays and spam filters check the HELO name, so this can cause rejections.

::diff{file="api/libs/smtp.py" lines="33-36"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The default path should be behavior-preserving. The override should only replace the server-name EHLO when it is actually set.

Suggested shape:

::suggestion{file="api/libs/smtp.py" lines="33-36"}
if self.use_tls and self.opportunistic_tls:
    ehlo_name = dify_config.SMTP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME or self.server
    smtp.ehlo(ehlo_name)
    smtp.starttls()
    smtp.ehlo(ehlo_name)

The tests were changed from `assert_called_once_with(..., timeout=10)` to `assert_called_once_with(..., timeout=10, local_hostname=ANY)`. `ANY` matches any value, including `None`, so these assertions only confirm the kwarg exists. Nothing checks that `SMTP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME` is actually used: not in the constructor, not in the opportunistic `ehlo` calls, and not the default fallback. The default-behavior regression above passes these tests unnoticed. The PR checklist says a test was added for each change, but the new feature has no test that sets the config.

::diff{file="api/tests/unit_tests/libs/test_smtp_client.py" lines="20-20"}

Add tests that patch `dify_config.SMTP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME` (or the `libs.smtp.dify_config` attribute) to a concrete value and assert that value reaches `SMTP(..., local_hostname="relay.internal")` and the `ehlo` calls in opportunistic mode. Add a companion test with the setting empty or None that asserts the default EHLO name is unchanged.

The TLS branching was rewritten as a parenthesized conditional expression selecting the class, followed by an `assert smtp is not None` used only to narrow the type for mypy. This refactor is not needed for the feature. The original explicit if/elif/else made each mode's connection and EHLO steps easy to read. The new form is harder to follow, and the assert is stripped under `python -O`. Keep the original branching and only add `local_hostname=` to each constructor call, or build the class and kwargs explicitly.

::diff{file="api/libs/smtp.py" lines="27-32"}

Also, the empty-string normalization is doubled: `local_host = ... or ""` and then `local_host or None` in the constructor call. One `local_hostname = dify_config.SMTP_LOCAL_HOSTNAME or None` value would be enough, since `ehlo(None)` already falls back to the local hostname.

The diff appends an empty line after `SANDBOX_EXPIRED_RECORDS_RETENTION_DAYS=30`, so the file now ends with a blank line (line 718 is empty). It is harmless, but it is unrelated to the feature and creates a trailing-whitespace/EOF diff noise that linters and other env examples in the repo don't carry.

::diff{file="api/.env.example" lines="715-718"}

Remove the trailing empty line so the file ends at the last `SANDBOX_...` entry.
